+# Implementation Plan: JSON Patch
+
+**Spec**: [spec.md](spec.md) | Standard: RFC 6902 §3–§5, RFC 6901 §3–§4
+
+## Approach
+Single module `src/index.ts` (the test runner executes TS directly, so no `.js` sibling imports). Extract pointer parsing from `resolvePointer` into an internal `parsePointer`, shared by both. `applyPatch` deep-clones the document (own clone that uses `defineProperty`, safe for `__proto__`), applies operations in place on the clone, and returns it; on any error the clone is dropped, giving atomicity. Values taken from the patch are cloned before insertion.
+
+## Constitution Check
+- I: RFC 6902 sections named; error rules (§4, §5) implemented exactly. Root `remove` rejected (no value results) — noted in spec.
+- II: no dependencies added.
+- III: tests in `test/patch.test.ts` written first and seen failing.
+- IV: no mutation, own-member checks, defineProperty for assignments, typed `JsonPatchError`.
+- V: strict TS, doc comments naming the standard, no `any`.
+- VI: pure helpers only.
