+# Feature Specification: JSON Patch
+
+**Created**: 2026-11-17 | **Status**: Draft
+**Input**: Implement JSON Patch as `applyPatch(document, patch)` with add, remove, replace, move, copy, test.
+**Standard**: RFC 6902 (JSON Patch) §3 document structure, §4.1-4.6 operations, §5 error handling; RFC 6901 pointers for `path`/`from`; equality for `test` per §4.6.
+
+## User Scenarios & Testing
+
+### User Story 1 - Apply a patch (P1)
+A service passes a document and a patch array and receives a new, patched document.
+
+**Independent Test**: every example of RFC 6902 Appendix A.
+
+**Acceptance Scenarios**:
+1. `add` to an object adds or replaces a member; to an array inserts before the index; `-` appends; index greater than length fails; `""` replaces the whole document (§4.1).
+2. `remove` and `replace` require the target to exist (§4.2, §4.3).
+3. `move` removes `from` and adds at `path`; `from` must exist and must not be a proper prefix of `path` (§4.4).
+4. `copy` adds a copy of the `from` value at `path` (§4.5).
+5. `test` succeeds if the value equals `value` (types must match, objects unordered, arrays ordered, numbers by value, `null` is a value); otherwise fails (§4.6).
+6. Operations are applied sequentially, each on the result of the previous one.
+
+### User Story 2 - Reject bad patches, atomically (P1)
+1. A patch that is not an array, an operation that is not an object, a missing/unknown `op`, a missing/non-string `path` or `from`, or a missing `value` (add, replace, test) throws `JsonPatchError`.
+2. A failing operation (missing target, bad index, failed test) throws `JsonPatchError`; the input is unchanged and no partial result is returned (§5).
+3. Invalid pointer syntax throws `JsonPatchError`.
+
+### Edge Cases
+- Inputs (document and patch) are never mutated; the result shares no structure with them.
+- `__proto__`, `constructor`, `prototype` keys are plain own members; they never touch prototypes. Inherited members are not targets.
+- Removing the whole document (`remove` with path `""`) is rejected: no JSON value would result.
+- Extra members in an operation are ignored (§4).
+
+## Requirements
+- **FR-001**: `applyPatch(document, patch)` exported from `src/index.ts`, returns a new document.
+- **FR-002**: Each operation follows RFC 6902 §4; errors throw `JsonPatchError`.
+- **FR-003**: Patch structure validated per §3/§4 before/while applying; whole patch is atomic (§5).
+- **FR-004**: No input mutation; prototype-pollution safe.
+- **FR-005**: `README.md` documents the function.
+
+## Assumptions
+- Documents are values as produced by JSON parsing.
